# um-texts 1
=== QITEM Danger_Sensor
Crystal
A good thing! Pity there's no one who could teach you how to use it, though...

=== QITEM Large_Potion_1
Healing potion - big vial
Restores a character's health almost completely.

=== QITEM Large_Potion_2
Strength potion - big vial
Increases a character's strength for a long period of time.

=== QITEM Large_Potion_3
Haste potion - big vial
Significantly increases a character's speed.

=== QITEM Potion_1
Healing potion - medium vial
Partially restores a character's health.

=== QITEM Potion_2
Strength potion - medium vial
Increases a character's strength.

=== QITEM Potion_3
Haste potion - medium vial
Increases a character's speed.

=== QITEM Potion_Enlarge
Enlargement elixir
Increases the size of those who drink it.

=== QITEM Potion_Shrink
Shrinking elixir
Decreases the size of those who drink it.

=== QITEM Small_Potion_1
Healing potion - small vial
Restores a small fraction of a character's health.

=== QITEM Small_Potion_2
Strength potion - small vial
Increases a character's strength for a short period of time.

=== QITEM Small_Potion_3
Haste potion - small vial
Increases a character's speed by a small measure.

=== QITEM Spell_Container
Something magical
A strange thing indeed... and there's no one who could even give a hint as to what it is for...

=== QITEM Tiny_Potion_1
Healing potion - very small vial
Restores a very small fraction of a character's health.

=== QITEM Tiny_Potion_2
Strength potion - very small vial
Increases a character's strength for a very limited period of time.

=== QITEM Tiny_Potion_3
Haste potion - very small vial
Increases a character's speed by a very small measure.

=== QITEM Wand_1 Granite
Granite wand
A bit better than stone but worse than all others.

=== QITEM Wand_1 Malachite
Obsidian wand
The best of stone wands.

=== QITEM Wand_1 Rock
Stone wand
The simplest and weakest of wands.

=== QITEM Wand_1 Silicon
Silicon wand
A decent stone wand.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Burned_bones
Hard bone wand
A good choice for a trained magician.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Decayed_bones
Thin bone wand
A simple bone wand.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Dragon_Black_Bones
Blue Dragon bone wand
Dragon bones enable one to use a very high level of magic.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Dragon_Green_Bones
Green Dragon bone wand
Dragon bones enable one to use a very high level of magic.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Dragon_Red_Bones
Red Dragon bone wand
Dragon bones enable one to use a very high level of magic.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Dry_bones
Tough bone wand
A decent bone wand.

=== QITEM Wand_2 Scrab_bones
Shell bone wand
Good material - gives good effect.

=== QITEM Wand_3 Adamantium
Adamantite wand
You can cast very powerful spells with this wand.

=== QITEM Wand_3 Bronze
Bronze wand
The simplest of metal wands. An experienced magician deserves something better.

=== QITEM Wand_3 Iron
Iron wand
Better than bronze, but worse than any other metal wand.

=== QITEM Wand_3 Meteoric
Meteorite wand
Only an experienced magician can fully use its potential!

=== QITEM Wand_3 Mithrill
Mithrill wand
Mithrill is light and strong and also absorbs magic wonderfully.

=== QITEM Wand_3 Steel
Steel wand
Steel doesn't just make good weapons.

=== QITEM Wand_4 Adamantium
Decorative adamantite wand
This one will shoot magic just as well as the adamantite crossbow shoots arrows.

=== QITEM Wand_4 Bronze
Decorative bronze wand
You could choose a more serious material for a decorative wand!

=== QITEM Wand_4 Iron
Decorative iron wand
It will work, but not well enough for a master magician.

=== QITEM Wand_4 Meteoric
Decorative meteorite wand
The best of all possible magic wands.

=== QITEM Wand_4 Mithrill
Decorative mithrill wand
Many magicians in this world dream about having one!

=== QITEM Wand_4 Steel
Decorative steel wand
Not a bad choice!

=== QITEM Wand_5 Dragon_Green_Bones
Green Dragon horn
A magical Dragon horn used by Lizards.

=== QITEM Wand_6 Rock
Goblin doll
A magical stone doll used by Goblins.

